    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nThose mappings are [documented](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/ecde5ffd9adfd590d5c2d5d35a7f0152def894fc/doc/mini-clue.txt#L93-L94) and chosen for a reason that they enhance default ones (both `Q` and `@` work with macros). They will not be configurable because I strongly believe that overriding either of them is not a good idea.\n\nAt the moment users can work around this by making custom mappings after `require('mini.clue').setup()`. As described in #619 and #998.\n\nI've originally made a neovim/neovim#24565 in the hope that it would eliminate the need for custom mappings, but as it has stalled, there should be a better default behavior indeed. Probably, creating those mappings only if user hasn't already overridden them is a better decision here. I'll work on that.",
